/* IID -> object type lookup                                           */
/* ================================================================== */
/*
 * Resolve a caller-supplied REFIID (e.g. the riid argument to
 * CreateDXGIFactory1 or IUnknown::QueryInterface) to the matching
 * NPT_OBJECT_TYPE_* value.  Returns NPT_OBJECT_TYPE_IUNKNOWN (= the
 * "untyped" sentinel) when the IID isn't one of the interfaces in
 * the registry -- the consumer's handle table treats IUNKNOWN as
 * permissive, so unknown IIDs don't cause a legitimate caller to
 * fail.
 *
 * Static table with linear search is fine here: ~200 interfaces,
 * only called on object-creation paths.
 */
